---
import { Terminal } from "@lucide/astro";
import { REPO } from "../../../config/site";
import CommandBlock from "../CommandBlock.astro";

const distributions = [
  {
    name: "Ubuntu / Debian / Linux Mint",
    note: "Ubuntu 22.04 or newer, Debian 12 or newer, and compatible Linux Mint releases. If a package cannot be found on Ubuntu, enable the Universe repository in Software & Updates, then run apt update again.",
    command: `sudo apt update
sudo apt install libwebkit2gtk-4.1-0 ca-certificates \\
  gstreamer1.0-tools gstreamer1.0-plugins-base \\
  gstreamer1.0-plugins-good gstreamer1.0-plugins-bad \\
  gstreamer1.0-plugins-ugly gstreamer1.0-libav \\
  gstreamer1.0-gl gstreamer1.0-pulseaudio pulseaudio-utils`,
    check: "dpkg-query -W libwebkit2gtk-4.1-0",
  },
  {
    name: "Arch Linux / EndeavourOS",
    note: "Keep Arch fully updated so WebKit, FFmpeg, libva, and GStreamer come from a consistent set of packages.",
    command: `sudo pacman -Syu --needed webkit2gtk-4.1 gstreamer \\
  gst-plugins-base gst-plugins-good gst-plugins-bad \\
  gst-plugins-ugly gst-libav libpulse`,
    check: "pacman -Q webkit2gtk-4.1",
  },
  {
    name: "Fedora",
    note: "These commands install Fedora's runtime and base plugins. Some H.264, HEVC, and other codec support may need additional packages; use Fedora's codec instructions linked below if decoder checks are missing.",
    command: `sudo dnf upgrade --refresh
sudo dnf install webkit2gtk4.1 gstreamer1 \\
  gstreamer1-plugins-base gstreamer1-plugins-good \\
  gstreamer1-plugins-bad-free gstreamer1-plugins-ugly-free \\
  pulseaudio-utils`,
    check: "rpm -q webkit2gtk4.1",
  },
];

const decoderCheck = `gst-inspect-1.0 --version
for element in qtdemux matroskademux h264parse h265parse avdec_h264 avdec_h265 avdec_aac autoaudiosink; do
  if gst-inspect-1.0 "$element" >/dev/null 2>&1; then
    printf 'PASS     %s\\n' "$element"
  else
    printf 'MISSING  %s\\n' "$element"
  fi
done`;
---

<section id="linux-setup" class="linux-guide rounded-2xl border border-white/10 bg-vega-surface p-5 sm:p-7 md:p-10">
  <div class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 rounded-full border border-white/15 bg-white/5 px-4 py-1.5 text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-widest text-vega-accent">
    <Terminal class="h-4 w-4" aria-hidden="true" /> Linux Setup
  </div>
  <h1 class="mt-4 font-headline text-[clamp(2rem,4vw,3.1rem)] font-black tracking-tight text-white">Get Linux ready for Vega</h1>
  <p class="mt-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-vega-muted">Install the desktop runtime and media plugins for your distribution, then run the checks below before playing a video.</p>

  <article class="mt-7 rounded-xl border border-white/10 bg-vega-surface-hi p-5">
    <h2>What your system needs</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>A graphical desktop session using X11 or Wayland, with working graphics drivers and sound.</li>
      <li>WebKitGTK 4.1 and its GTK runtime for Vega's desktop interface.</li>
      <li>GStreamer media plugins for the built-in player, including decoders for the files you watch.</li>
      <li>A Vega build that matches your CPU architecture.</li>
    </ul>
    <CommandBlock label="Identify your distribution and CPU" command={`cat /etc/os-release
uname -m`} />
    <p>Match <code>x86_64</code> to an <code>amd64</code>/<code>x86_64</code> asset, or <code>aarch64</code> to an <code>arm64</code> asset if that release provides one.</p>
  </article>

  <h2 class="mt-9" id="runtime-packages">1. Install your runtime packages</h2>
  <p>Open Terminal and choose your distribution. These are runtime packages for running Vega. Your package manager will also install their dependencies.</p>
  <div class="mt-4 space-y-3">
    {distributions.map((distribution, index) => (
      <details class="rounded-xl border border-white/10 bg-vega-surface-hi p-4 sm:p-5" open={index === 0}>
        <summary class="cursor-pointer font-headline text-lg font-bold text-white marker:text-vega-accent">{distribution.name}</summary>
        <p>{distribution.note}</p>
        <CommandBlock label={`Install packages — ${distribution.name}`} command={distribution.command} />
        <CommandBlock label={`Confirm WebKitGTK — ${distribution.name}`} command={distribution.check} />
        <p>Expected: the installed WebKitGTK package and its version. A “not installed” result means the runtime is still missing.</p>
        {distribution.name === "Fedora" && <p><a href="https://docs.fedoraproject.org/en-US/quick-docs/installing-plugins-for-playing-movies-and-music/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Fedora's multimedia codec instructions →</a></p>}
      </details>
    ))}
  </div>

  <h2 class="mt-9" id="install-vega">2. Install Vega</h2>
  <p>Download the latest matching asset from the <a href={REPO.releasesUrl} target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">official desktop releases</a>. Run the relevant command from the folder containing your download, with only one matching Vega installer in that folder.</p>
  <CommandBlock label="Ubuntu / Debian — install the .deb" command="sudo apt install ./Vega_*.deb" />
  <CommandBlock label="Fedora — install the .rpm" command="sudo dnf install ./Vega*.rpm" />
  <p>Launch Vega from your applications menu as your normal desktop user.</p>

  <details class="mt-5 rounded-xl border border-white/10 bg-vega-surface-hi p-5">
    <summary class="cursor-pointer font-headline text-lg font-bold text-white marker:text-vega-accent">Using an AppImage instead?</summary>
    <CommandBlock label="Make the AppImage executable and launch it" command={`chmod +x ./Vega_*.AppImage
./Vega_*.AppImage`} />
    <p>If it reports a FUSE error, install the FUSE 2 library for your distribution:</p>
    <CommandBlock label="Ubuntu 24.04+ / Debian 13+" command="sudo apt install libfuse2t64" />
    <CommandBlock label="Ubuntu 22.04 / Debian 12" command="sudo apt install libfuse2" />
    <CommandBlock label="Arch Linux" command="sudo pacman -S fuse2" />
    <CommandBlock label="Fedora" command="sudo dnf install fuse-libs" />
    <p>See the <a href="https://docs.appimage.org/user-guide/troubleshooting/fuse.html" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">AppImage FUSE guide</a> for other distributions.</p>
  </details>

  <h2 class="mt-9" id="confirm-playback">3. Confirm video and audio support</h2>
  <CommandBlock label="Check GStreamer and common video/audio elements" command={decoderCheck} />
  <p><strong>PASS</strong> means that element can be loaded. <strong>MISSING</strong> means it is unavailable or failed to load; install the relevant media plugins for your distribution. <code>avdec_h264</code>, <code>avdec_h265</code>, and <code>avdec_aac</code> check software decoders for H.264, HEVC, and AAC. Other decoders may also support those formats.</p>
  <CommandBlock label="Confirm your session's audio server" command="pactl info" />
  <p>Expected: server details, including <strong>Server Name</strong> and <strong>Default Sink</strong>. PulseAudio and PipeWire's PulseAudio compatibility service both work. A connection error means this command cannot reach your session's audio server; check your desktop sound settings and that service before testing playback.</p>
  <p>Finally, play a local file in Vega. Confirm that time advances, sound works, audio tracks switch, and resizing stays responsive. Press <kbd>F11</kbd> to enter fullscreen and <kbd>Esc</kbd> to exit. Component checks alone do not guarantee every codec profile or GPU path will play correctly.</p>

  <h2 class="mt-9" id="troubleshooting">If a check fails</h2>
  <div class="mt-4 space-y-4">
    <article class="rounded-xl border border-white/10 bg-vega-surface-hi p-5">
      <h3>“undefined symbol: vaMapBuffer2” or another library error</h3>
      <p>This indicates incompatible loaded libraries, rather than establishing a missing HEVC decoder. Update your distribution's packages together and relaunch the latest Vega build. On Arch, use a full <code>sudo pacman -Syu</code> update. If the error remains, include the complete error line and the executable/library paths when reporting it.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="rounded-xl border border-white/10 bg-vega-surface-hi p-5">
      <h3>FFmpeg / FFprobe checks</h3>
      <p>Vega's packaged FFmpeg and FFprobe handle probing and remuxing; GStreamer plugins are separate. Checking a system <code>ffprobe</code> alone does not confirm Vega's bundled tool works. For a current installed .deb, check the bundled tool directly:</p>
      <CommandBlock label="Confirm the bundled FFprobe starts (.deb)" command="/usr/lib/Vega/resources/ffmpeg-sidecar/ffprobe -version" />
      <p>Expected: FFprobe's version and build information. If that file is missing, check your installed package/version. AppImage and other package layouts can use a different path.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="rounded-xl border border-white/10 bg-vega-surface-hi p-5">
      <h3>The whole app freezes, but the checks pass</h3>
      <p>Report the Vega version, distribution/version, GPU, whether the problem affects local files or streams, and exported Vega logs. A working decoder check or playback in VLC does not identify the cause of a WebKit playback freeze.</p>
    </article>
  </div>
  <p class="mt-7 text-xs">Package references: <a href="https://v2.tauri.app/distribute/debian/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Tauri Linux runtime</a> · <a href="https://gstreamer.freedesktop.org/documentation/installing/on-linux.html" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">GStreamer installation</a> · <a href="https://archlinux.org/packages/extra/x86_64/gst-libav/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Arch libav plugin</a></p>
</section>

<style>
  .linux-guide h2 { font-family: var(--font-headline); font-size: 1.35rem; font-weight: 700; color: white; line-height: 1.4; }
  .linux-guide h3 { font-family: var(--font-headline); font-size: 1.05rem; font-weight: 700; color: white; }
  .linux-guide p { margin-top: .8rem; color: var(--color-vega-muted); font-size: .9rem; line-height: 1.8; }
  .linux-guide ul { margin-top: .8rem; padding-left: 1.2rem; list-style: disc; color: var(--color-vega-muted); font-size: .9rem; line-height: 1.8; }
  .linux-guide li + li { margin-top: .35rem; }
  .linux-guide a { color: var(--color-vega-accent); text-decoration: underline; text-underline-offset: 3px; }
  .linux-guide strong { color: white; font-weight: 600; }
  .linux-guide p code, .linux-guide li code, .linux-guide kbd { border-radius: .25rem; background: rgb(255 255 255 / .07); padding: .1rem .3rem; color: white; font-size: .85em; overflow-wrap: anywhere; }
</style>
